60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option C is too risky; the non-refundable deposit and high transport costs for a distant lodge are financial liabilities we can't afford. Option B is impractical due to the hall's schedule and commute issues. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shion,,"Option A is a nightmare for recovery with eight people to a room and strict curfews. Option B is a scheduling disaster. Despite the risks, Option C is the only one that ensures proper rest and training. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minato,,Option A sounds like a lot of work for the organizers with that application process. Option B means someone has to cook. Option C seems the most peaceful for everyone. I vote for Option C.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Option A is cheap, but the lottery is a gamble. Option B is a logistical mess. Option C is tempting for the staff, but the financial risk of non-refundable deposits is too high. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"Option B is out because we can't all be there together. Option A is just a barracks. If we want to actually bond and fix the club, we need Option C. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shion, @Minato, @Takumi, you are prioritizing comfort and bonding over financial stability. If we choose C and people drop out, the remaining members pay the price. That is not a sustainable way to run a club.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shion"",""Minato"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, sustainability also means maintaining the quality of our training. If we choose A, we are essentially paying for a camp where members are exhausted and miserable. That is a waste of resources in its own right.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Asuka, I understand the money is important, but if the organizers are too tired to train or the application is too stressful, it's not a good camp. Option C lets us all focus on the training and each other.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Asuka, I agree that the financial risk is the primary concern. If we choose C and attendance drops as it did last year, the deficit will be unavoidable. Option A is the only fiscally responsible choice.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Misaki, @Asuka, you're so worried about the money that you're willing to let the club's spirit die. If we keep picking the ""safe"" option, we'll just keep losing members. Option C is the only way to actually save this club.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, spirit doesn't pay the bills. If we bankrupt the club account with a non-refundable deposit for people who don't show up, there will be no club left to save. We must prioritize stability.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, stability is useless if the training is ineffective. Option A's conditions are a recipe for failure. We are a sports club, not a military camp. Option C is the only logical choice for performance.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minato,,"@Asuka, @Misaki, I really don't want anyone to be stressed. If we pick Option A, the organizers will be overwhelmed by the paperwork and the lottery. Option C is the only one where everyone can actually relax.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Minato, I understand the stress of paperwork, but the stress of a financial deficit is far worse. We cannot gamble with the club's funds on a venue where we pay for empty beds. Option A is the safest.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Misaki, @Asuka, you're treating this like a math problem, but it's about people. If we don't invest in a place where we actually live and breathe as a team, we're just delaying the end. I'm sticking with Option C.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, @Shion, @Minato, I cannot ignore the data on transport costs and deposits. While I value the club's spirit, financial ruin is a permanent failure. I maintain my vote for Option A.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Shion"",""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, your fear of a deficit is noted, but the cost of a failed camp is higher. We cannot sacrifice our performance for a budget. I stand by my vote for Option C.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Minato,,I really hope we can choose the one that's kindest to everyone. I don't want the organizers to be exhausted or stressed. I'm staying with my vote for Option C.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"I cannot support a gamble with our funds. Given the attendance trends and the risk of non-refundable deposits, Option C is too dangerous. I must prioritize the club's financial survival. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, @Misaki, you're choosing a budget over the people. If we don't fix the divide in this club now, there won't be anyone left to manage that account. I'm voting for Option C.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
